DataRange [SimTalk]
Sets the data range, which the objects table of the Chart designated by <Path> uses.
Remarks
The data range applies for these settings.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.DataRange:string
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type string.
Example
MyChart.DataRange := "{*,*}..{*,*}    // no limitations
MyChart.DataRange := "{1,1}..{1,4}"   // designates the first four rowns in 
the first column
MyChart.DataRange := "{1,1}..{1,*}"   // designates the entire first column
MyChart.DataRange := "{-2,*}..{-2,*}" // designates the one but last column 
DataTable
MyChart.DataRange := "{-2,*}..{*,*}"  // designates the two last columns of 
the DataTable
DataRange [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 11-4765
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

See also
Data Source [Chart]
