ImageQuality3D [SimTalk]
Sets the image quality with which the image of the Chart designated by <Path> is shown in the Frame.
Remarks
ImageQuality3D applies if you assigned true to the attribute DisplayInFrame. Then you can select the 3D
Image Quality with which the Chart shows the image in 3D. The 3D Image Quality is only active in a 3D
model.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.ImageQuality3D:string
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type string.
You can specify:
• "High quality" results in high resolution and improved image quality with bad performance.
• "Balanced" results in medium resolution, is a good compromise between image quality and
performance.
• "High performance" results in low resolution and bad image quality with better performance.
Example
MyChart.ImageQuality3D := "Balanced"
SimTalk
DisplayInFrame [SimTalk]
See also
3D Image Quality [drop-down list]
Display in Frame [check box] - Chart
ImageQuality3D [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 11-4775
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

InputChannels [SimTalk]
Designates a table containing the definitions of all input channels of the Chart designated by <Path>.
Remarks
When you assign a table to InputChannels with the assignment operator :=, Plant Simulation deactivates
inheritance.
Any other kind of writing access, as shown in the example above, does not deactivate inheritance. This
means that one of these accesses changes the table which the input channels table shares with its origin.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.InputChannels:table
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type table.
Example
MyChart.InputChannels.delete
MyChart.InputChannels.insertList(1,1,table.copy)
MyChart.Inputchannels := MyDataTable.copy({0,0}..{*,*})
print MyChart.InputChannels[1,1]
See also
Data Source [Chart]
InputChannels [SimTalk]
11-4776 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

