XGridlines [SimTalk]
Sets the number of grid lines that the Chart designated by <Path> shows on the x-axis.
Remarks
The Chart also shows a label for each grid line on the x-axis. If you are displaying a large number of data
sets, it makes sense to enter a smaller number so that the labels can be shown completely.
If the number of grid lines is greater than the number of data sets on the x-axis, the Chart only shows as
many grid lines as there are data sets. If the number of grid lines is smaller than the number of data sets,
the Chart reduces the number of grid lines and labels.
Note
If you select the Category > XY-Graph, the Chart only evaluates the Number if you also enter a fixed
Range X, i.e., if you did not enter an asterisk *.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.XGridlines:integer
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type integer.
Example
MyChart.XGridlines := 10
See also
Number of grid lines
Category [drop-down list]
Range X
XGridlines [SimTalk]
