YGridLineInterval [SimTalk]
Sets the interval between the grid lines on the y-axis of the Chart designated by <Path>.
Remarks
YGridLineInterval sets the distance of the horizontal grid lines and the labels on the y-axis.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.YGridLineInterval:real
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type real.
Specify 0 to make Plant Simulation determine a meaningful interval based on the displayed values.
Example
MyChart.YGridLineInterval := 2
See also
Interval
YGridLineInterval [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 11-4809
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

YLabel [SimTalk]
Sets the label of the y-axis that the Chart designated by <Path> shows in the Chart window.
Remarks
Applies to the 3D chart types 3D Columns, 3D Wire Frame, and 3D Surface.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
